{"name":"Snowberry","hex":"#efeced","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"snowberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub bearing white berries:\nnow especially of the genus Symphoricarpos, of North America\nwintergreen, of genus Gaultheria, especially Gaultheria oppositifolia, and\n Australian crabapple (Schizomeria ovata)","now especially of the genus Symphoricarpos, of North America"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snowberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Symphoricarpos","blocks":[{"text":"Symphoricarpos is a small genus of about 15 species of deciduous shrubs in the family Caprifoliaceae. With the exception of the Chinese coralberry, S. sinensis, which is indigenous to western China, all species are native to North and Central America. The name of the genus is derived from the Ancient Greek words συμφορεῖν (sumphoreîn), meaning \"to bear together\", and καρπός (karpós), meaning \"fruit\". It refers to the closely packed clusters of berries the species produces. Species in the genus are known by several common names, including snowberry, waxberry and ghostberry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Symphoricarpos_albus_7927.jpg/330px-Symphoricarpos_albus_7927.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symphoricarpos","wikidata":"Q157972"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Symphoricarpos_albus_3049.JPG/120px-Symphoricarpos_albus_3049.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Symphoricarpos_albus_3049.JPG/250px-Symphoricarpos_albus_3049.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Symphoricarpos_albus_3049.JPG/120px-Symphoricarpos_albus_3049.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser